# f1 = heavy, f2 = falls, f3 = light, f4 = holdsHeavy, f5 = holdsFalls, f6 = holdsLight
# A short loop that stands in no other is left a loop where it holds a call that loops alone copy: as a loop it holds one copy. Whether loops copy the callee was asked by its size, up to forty operations. The inliner is finer: by size alone it copies up to twenty-four in a loop, and some bodies it does not walk in line at all. For those the loop stayed a loop AND the callee stayed a call: the turns written out were taken away and nothing was given.
# The question is the inliner's own. A callee of twenty-eight operations that is handed nothing which would pay for its copy: the turns are written out, three calls in straight code,
